<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $59.1 mln Dec 6.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $59.1 mln Dec 6.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $59.1 million surplus on December 6 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON DECEMBER 6</p>
<p>Exports: $196.3 million</p>
<p>Imports: $176.2 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $303.5 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $264.5 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $59.1 million</p>
<p>DECEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $978 million</p>
<p>Imports: $902 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.201 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $818 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $459 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2485418</p>
